{
 "meta": {
  "title": "Seating plan - House of Representatives chamber, 44th Parliament",
  "planDate": "12 November 2013",
  "source": "House of Representatives seating plan PDF ('House of Representatives Seating plan, 12 November 2013' per the document title; Adobe InDesign CS6 file created 7 November 2013; footer 'Serjeant-at-Arms … 12 November 2013') - the first revision of the 44th Parliament, prepared for its opening sitting. No archived capture of this exact revision survives (the seating-plan URL family is first captured in late 2013 only for its NEXT revision, and this file's own set first appears in 2019 - CDX index checked 25 October 2026), so the PDF's own metadata anchors the file (local file cand-a.pdf, sha256 c2b2d6fa24ac1fd2ca852316890acb163b0b763100982b86d9470a0dd195d650) - but the transcription is CORROBORATED by the archived next revision: Wayback Machine capture 20140212213707 of the same media-library seating.ashx URL serves the plan redrawn for the first December sittings (footer 'Serjeant-at-Arms … 2 December 2013', FORTY FOURTH head, sha256 e3809d70ab4ec7f6fa65c18fc612aa33209221b56f05b9c6d646b71a3f4a346d; transcribed alongside this one). Seat-for-seat against this file, that revision prints exactly the same plan except that (a) Griffith is VACANT (Kevin Rudd resigned on 13 November 2013; the second page's members index lists 'VACANT - Griffith'), (b) Bronwyn Bishop's label has moved from row 2 of the government ranks to directly beneath the chair, with Bruce Scott's moved to her former position, and (c) eleven further members are re-seated (Chalmers, Thomson, Snowdon, Griffin, Chesters, Mitchell, Giles, Claydon up/across the opposition rows, and Bandt from the government side's curve to the opposition side) - everything else matches at identical label coordinates (121 seats to within 0.5 pt, the remaining 17 to text-reflow distance) with identical party tallies once the Griffith vacancy is removed.",
  "harvested": "2026-10-25",
  "method": "PDF text layer (pdftotext -bbox-layout) parsed into surname/electorate label pairs by edge alignment (including a wrap-repair pass for the two-line 'Melbourne / Ports' electorate); every label cross-verified against (a) a macOS Vision OCR pass of the rasterised page (139/150 directly, the eleven arm/edge labels closed by 400-dpi crops - 150/150 agreement) and (b) the 2013-election roster in this repo (map/data/res-2013.json, year=2013 entries) for full names and parties as elected (150/150 match).",
  "page": "A4 portrait, 595.276 x 841.89 pt, single page (unlike the later InDesign revisions, this PDF carries no alphabetical member-index page). The chamber is drawn with the Speaker's chair at the top (north), the table running south from it, the government on the Speaker's right (the page's LEFT), the opposition on the left (page RIGHT), crossbench around the far (south) curve.",
  "geometry": "Five concentric rows of seats about a centre near (297.6, 535); row radii 88.51, 134.17, 175.8, 216.03, 257.71 pt. Arm seats span x ~ 38..200 on the government (left) side and x ~ 368..548 on the opposition (right) side, the outer rows reaching further towards the page edges. The front row's arms extend furthest north toward the Speaker. Seat coordinates below give the surname label's north-west corner in page points, y increasing downward. The chair itself - the 'SPEAKER' label at (287.4, 208.5) - carries no member's label on this revision.",
  "ordering": "Within each row, 'seat' numbers run from the northern (Speaker) end of the government side, around the far (south) curve, up to the northern end of the opposition side.",
  "corroboratedBy": {
